        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5253229e-5b67-562b-b07c-ec028078c733",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stacey McClean, Biff Byford, Frankie Sandford, Jay Asforis, Daisy Evans, Calvin Goldspink, Aaron Renfree, Hannah Richings, Rochelle Wiseman, Steve Dawson, Pete Gill, Graham Oliver, Paul Quinn\n- Organizations: S Club 8, Saxon\n- Events: S Club Search\n- Products: \"Princess of the Night\", Denim and Leather\n\nFacts:\n- Biff Byford, born Peter Rodney Byford on 15 January 1951, is an English singer best known as the lead singer of Saxon.\n- In 1981, Saxon released \"Princess of the Night\" as the opening track and a single from the album Denim and Leather.\n- \"Princess of the Night\" was written collectively by Saxon members Biff Byford, Steve Dawson, Pete Gill, Graham Oliver, and Paul Quinn.\n- In 2001, Stacey McClean and the other future S Club 8 members were chosen from thousands of hopefuls on the television series S Club Search.\n- The S Club 8 members chosen on S Club Search were Frankie Sandford, Jay Asforis, Daisy Evans, Calvin Goldspink, Stacey McClean, Aaron Renfree, Hannah Richings, and Rochelle Wiseman.\n- The selected S Club 8 members were all in their early teens or younger at the time they were chosen.\n- Stacey McClean, born on 17 February 1989, is an English solo singer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a15c5ad5-07d2-5fa7-921f-3e3e51784d28",
        "text": "Page: Stacey McClean. Sentence: Stacey McClean (born 17 February 1989) is an English solo singer.\nPage: Biff Byford. Sentence: Peter Rodney \"Biff\" Byford (born 15 January 1951) is an English singer best known as the lead singer of the heavy metal band Saxon.\nPage: S Club 8. Sentence: The group's members, Frankie Sandford, Jay Asforis, Daisy Evans, Calvin Goldspink, Stacey McClean, Aaron Renfree, Hannah Richings, and Rochelle Wiseman were all in their early teens or younger when they were chosen from thousands of hopefuls on the television series \"S Club Search\" in 2001.\nPage: Princess of the Night. Sentence: \"Princess of the Night\" is a single by British heavy metal band Saxon, featured as the opening track and single from their 1981 album \"Denim and Leather\"; the song was written as a group production of all five members of the band at the time: Peter \"Biff\" Byford, Steve Dawson, Pete Gill, Graham Oliver, and Paul Quinn.",
